# Raw and staging data are never committed (design spec §10: publish code and
# derived aggregates, never restricted raw extracts).
data/raw/
data/staging/
# A landed release that is deliberately *not* adopted lives here, not under data/raw/. A vintage in the
# raw layer is a claim that it has been parsed and gated, and `tests/verify_quality.py` fails on a landed
# document the parsed artifact does not read - so "downloaded but unadopted" needs its own place.
data/pending/

# The analytical base is a build artifact, not source: reproducible from data/raw/ plus the
# declared rules in analysis/specs/. Committing the DuckDB file would ship a binary that can
disagree with the specs without anyone noticing.
data/*.duckdb
data/*.duckdb.wal

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.env
.ruff_cache/

# Scratch probes. Reconnaissance scripts and downloaded pages used to answer one question; they are
# not evidence and must not become part of the record by accident. Kept on disk, never committed.
.probe/

# Browser-pass screenshots. A screenshot is a way of looking at a page, not a record of it: the page
# is rebuilt from registry/ and the specs, and a captured PNG of a stale build is worse than no
# evidence at all. Root-level and .inspect/ captures stay on disk, never in the history.
/*.png
.inspect/*.png

# One-question probes and the exploratory pilots under .inspect/. Their declared equivalents are
# tracked: a probe that matters becomes a script in scripts/ with a spec in analysis/specs/.
.inspect/pilot_*
.inspect/probe_*
.inspect/export_*.py
.inspect/c_gaps.py
.inspect/u5mr_panel.csv

# Derived exploratory outputs. The panel, the fits and the placebo distributions are reproducible from
# data/analytics.duckdb plus analysis/specs/design_c_prime.yml, so committing them would put a second copy
# of a number in the repo, free to disagree with the spec that produced it. The command that rebuilds them
# is named in docs/causal-phases.md.
.inspect/design_c_prime_*
.inspect/*.log

# Browser-automation session artifacts (playwright-cli). These hold page snapshots, and a
# snapshot of a credential-issuing page holds the credential — one such file captured the FRED
# API key on 2026-10-11. Never commit them.
.playwright-cli/
.playwright-mcp/

# R / renv — library is local, renv.lock IS committed
renv/library/
renv/staging/
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory

# The guided-flow site is a build artifact: `python site/build.py` writes it from registry/ and
# analysis/specs/. Committing it would put a second copy of every published number in the repo, free to
# disagree with the artifacts it was generated from.
site/dist/

# dbt
dbt/target/
dbt/logs/
dbt/dbt_packages/
# dbt writes this itself: a machine-local anonymous usage id, not project config.
dbt/.user.yml

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local machine inventory and agent tooling — deliberately NOT published.
# TOOLING.md describes this workstation (host, user, drives, env paths) and carries
# security notes about exposed credentials; `.agents/` is harness boilerplate, not project code.
# Remove these two lines if you do want them public.
TOOLING.md
.agents/

# Browser-pass screenshots taken while reviewing a page (playwright output). Not evidence.
shots/

# The demo's intermediate per-shot clips. The stills and the finished mp4 are committed; the encodes that
# assembled them are not, because they rebuild from the stills with `python tools/build_demo.py`.
docs/demo/build/

# The demo's soundtrack. The finished cut is committed for the README to play; the source recordings are not
# redistributed, so they stay on the machine that made the video.
*.m4a

